  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under Bankruptcy Code Section 548, the trustee can avoid a fraudulent transfer made within two years before filing if it was made for less than reasonably equivalent value while the debtor was insolvent or became insolvent. Selling a $200,000 home for $10,000 to a family member clearly fails the reasonably equivalent value test.
Wrong (A): Equitable subordination under Section 510(c) reorders claim priority for creditor misconduct; it does not recover transferred property.
Wrong (B): A preference under Section 547 involves payment on an existing debt to a creditor, not a below-value asset transfer to a family member.
Wrong (D): Lien avoidance under Sections 522(f) or 545 removes liens from property; it does not address pre-petition transfers of assets.$EXPL$
