  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under Section 547(b)(3), a preference requires that the debtor was insolvent at the time of the transfer. If the debtor was solvent when the payment was made, a key element of the preference test fails and the trustee cannot recover it regardless of other factors.
Wrong (B): While the 90-day window is a necessary condition under Section 547(b)(4)(A), meeting the timing requirement alone is insufficient if other elements such as insolvency are not satisfied.
Wrong (C): There is no $5,000 threshold in Section 547; the statute applies to transfers of any amount that meet all five statutory elements.
