  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under IRC Sec. 56(b)(3), the bargain element on ISO exercise -- the excess of fair market value over the exercise price -- is an AMT adjustment added to alternative minimum taxable income. Although Sec. 421(a) excludes this amount from regular income tax, the exclusion does not apply for AMT purposes.
Wrong (B): The AMT adjustment is triggered at exercise, not at sale; waiting until disposition would defeat the purpose of the AMT timing adjustment.
Wrong (C): Only the spread between FMV and exercise price is included, not the full fair market value of the shares.
