  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under IRC Section 56(b)(1)(A), state and local tax deductions -- including state income taxes and property taxes -- must be added back when computing AMTI. The AMT disallows this deduction to ensure taxpayers with large SALT deductions pay a minimum level of tax.
Wrong (A): Home mortgage interest on acquisition indebtedness for a primary residence is generally allowed for both regular tax and AMT purposes and is not an AMT add-back.
Wrong (B): Investment interest expense to the extent of net investment income is deductible for both regular tax and AMT, so no add-back is required.
