  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under IRC Sec. 55(b)(1), the individual AMT uses a two-tier rate structure: 26% on the first portion of AMTI above the exemption amount and 28% on AMTI exceeding the $232,600 threshold for single filers. This is simpler than the regular tax''s seven brackets.
Wrong (A): The 10% and 25% rates are brackets within the regular individual income tax system and have no application to the AMT computation.
Wrong (B): The 15% and 35% rates also belong to the regular income tax bracket schedule, not to the AMT rate structure.
Wrong (C): The 22% and 37% rates are regular income tax brackets; the AMT intentionally uses only two rates (26% and 28%) to ensure minimum taxation.$EXPL$
