  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under IRC Sec. 53, AMT paid due to timing (deferral) items like ISO exercises generates a minimum tax credit (MTC) carried forward indefinitely. In Year 2, when the regular tax exceeds the tentative minimum tax, the taxpayer can apply the MTC to reduce regular tax liability.
Wrong (A): The AMT is not lost; Sec. 53 specifically provides the MTC mechanism to prevent permanent double taxation on timing differences.
