-- Q5129: Estate and Gift Tax [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under IRC Section 1015(d)(6), the donee''s basis equals the donor''s basis plus the portion of gift tax attributable to net appreciation. Appreciation is $200,000 ($320,000 FMV minus $120,000 basis). The adjustment is $40,000 x ($200,000 / $320,000) = $25,000. Drake''s basis is $120,000 + $25,000 = $145,000.
Wrong (A): $120,000 is the donor''s unadjusted basis and ignores the gift tax basis adjustment required by Section 1015(d)(6).
Wrong (B): $320,000 is the fair market value; a donee''s basis in gifted property is not stepped up to FMV (that rule applies to inherited property under Section 1014).
Wrong (C): $160,000 incorrectly adds the full $40,000 gift tax to the donor''s basis rather than only the portion allocable to the net appreciation.$EXPL$
